      "message": "Draw the welcome steps as a stepper, and put \"Your page\" where you live\n\nThe welcome page's rail of steps shared its class with the front page's\n\"Push. Prove. Land.\" strip, so the strip's animated line ran across the\nfirst step. The rail has classes of its own now, and it is drawn as a\nstepper: three nodes joined by a line, the current one in the accent\nwith a soft ring, the ones behind it filled and ticked, the line between\nthem coloured as far as you have come.\n\nThe username on the first step ran its label, value and note together;\nit is a labelled fact now, with the note beneath.\n\nThe account menu at the foot of the sidebar opens with \"Your page\": the\none place that already holds everything about you, so your own page is\na click away from anywhere rather than an address to type.\n\nChange-Id: Iwelcome0172\nTask: t-2rns0dgs2p1szdg7yagj2fkcmt\nSigned-off-by: Mandip Adhikari <92096340+mandipadk@users.noreply.github.com>",
